additional_notes:
Alone, "il vu" is ungrammatical. If you see it in text, check for a missing auxiliary verb (e.g. "a" or "est") or for omitted punctuation. Related correct forms:
- "il a vu" = "he saw / he has seen";
- "il est vu" = passive "he/it is seen";
- "Vu le rapport..." = "Given the report..." (formal/legal).

This sequence alone is ungrammatical in standard French. Possible intended forms:
- «vous tous» or «vous, tous» = 'all of you';
- «tous les…/toutes les…» or «tout le…/toute la…» = 'all the…' (followed by a noun);
- «vous, tout le…» might appear when addressing someone then continuing with 'the whole…' but requires completion. Use «vous tous» (or «vous toutes» for an all-female group) to say 'you all'.
